Package: data.table.ext
Type: Package
Title: Enhanced Display, Sampling, and Database Querying for 'data.table'
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Kyle", "Haynes", email = "kyle@kylehaynes.com.au", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Darko", "Bergant", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "author of datamodelr (MIT), which the data model and diagram code is ported from"))
Description: Adds opt-in data.table output enhancements for printing, grouped
    sampling, and data.table-focused str() and dput() behavior, including
    helpers for grouped value highlighting and readability improvements.
    Also provides a data.table-style '[i, j, by]' interface backed by
    'DuckDB' and Microsoft SQL Server, translating expressions to SQL and
    executing them in the database so data stays there until the result is
    materialized as a data.table. Also reverse-engineers a database into a
    data model -- tables, columns, keys and references -- and draws it as an
    interactive entity-relationship diagram that builds the query for the
    tables and columns you pick.
